---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="SmartBoardAI — Eliana Betancur"
    description="A full-stack AI-powered project planning application built as a capstone project at DePaul University."
>
    <div class="px-6 sm:px-10 pt-8 pb-20">
        <article class="w-full page-reveal">
            <p
                class="font-mono font-medium text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-rust-700 mb-5 flex items-center gap-3"
            >
                <span
                    class="inline-block w-2.5 h-2.5 bg-rust-500"
                    aria-hidden="true"></span>
                Capstone Project — Full Stack + AI
            </p>

            <h1
                class="font-display font-bold text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl leading-[1.1] mb-6"
            >
                SmartBoardAI
            </h1>

            <p
                class="font-sans text-lg sm:text-xl text-warmgray-600 leading-relaxed mb-12"
            >
                An AI-powered project planning application that turns
                plain-language ideas into structured, actionable project plans —
                built end to end by a four-person team for my DePaul University
                capstone.
            </p>

            <div
                class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-4 mb-16 py-8 border-t border-b border-warmgray-300"
            >
                <div>
                    <p
                        class="font-mono text-xs text-warmgray-500 uppercase tracking-widest mb-1"
                    >
                        Role
                    </p>
                    <p class="font-sans text-sm text-warmgray-800 font-medium">
                        UX, Frontend, Team Lead
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <p
                        class="font-mono text-xs text-warmgray-500 uppercase tracking-widest mb-1"
                    >
                        Context
                    </p>
                    <p class="font-sans text-sm text-warmgray-800 font-medium">
                        DePaul Capstone
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <p
                        class="font-mono text-xs text-warmgray-500 uppercase tracking-widest mb-1"
                    >
                        Timeline
                    </p>
                    <p class="font-sans text-sm text-warmgray-800 font-medium">
                        Fall 2025
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <p
                        class="font-mono text-xs text-warmgray-500 uppercase tracking-widest mb-1"
                    >
                        Stack
                    </p>
                    <p class="font-sans text-sm text-warmgray-800 font-medium">
                        React, Java, Python, MySQL
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <section class="mb-14">
                <h2
                    class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-warmgray-800 mb-4"
                >
                    The problem
                </h2>
                <p
                    class="font-sans text-base text-warmgray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4"
                >
                    Project planning tools require users to manually create,
                    categorize, and prioritize every task from scratch. For
                    students, freelancers, and small teams, this setup cost
                    creates real friction before any actual work begins.
                </p>
                <p
                    class="font-sans text-base text-warmgray-600 leading-relaxed"
                >
                    We wanted to build something that could take a
                    plain-language idea and turn it into a structured,
                    prioritized project plan in minutes — removing the setup
                    barrier entirely and letting people focus on execution.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-14">
                <h2
                    class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-warmgray-800 mb-6"
                >
                    What we built
                </h2>
                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                    <div class="bg-warmgray-200 rounded-lg p-6">
                        <p
                            class="font-mono text-xs text-rust-700 uppercase tracking-widest mb-3"
                        >
                            AI project generation
                        </p>
                        <p
                            class="font-sans text-sm text-warmgray-800 leading-relaxed"
                        >
                            Users describe an idea in plain language. The AI
                            middleware interprets the input and generates tasks,
                            priorities, and milestones automatically through a
                            conversational interface.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-warmgray-200 rounded-lg p-6">
                        <p
                            class="font-mono text-xs text-rust-700 uppercase tracking-widest mb-3"
                        >
                            Interactive Kanban board
                        </p>
                        <p
                            class="font-sans text-sm text-warmgray-800 leading-relaxed"
                        >
                            A drag-and-drop board with real-time status updates,
                            color-coded priorities, and category tags. Built in
                            React with live synchronization across team members.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-warmgray-200 rounded-lg p-6">
                        <p
                            class="font-mono text-xs text-rust-700 uppercase tracking-widest mb-3"
                        >
                            Full-stack architecture
                        </p>
                        <p
                            class="font-sans text-sm text-warmgray-800 leading-relaxed"
                        >
                            React and TypeScript frontend, Java Spring Boot
                            backend, Python FastAPI AI middleware, and MySQL
                            database — each layer designed for modularity and
                            scalability.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-warmgray-200 rounded-lg p-6">
                        <p
                            class="font-mono text-xs text-rust-700 uppercase tracking-widest mb-3"
                        >
                            Team collaboration
                        </p>
                        <p
                            class="font-sans text-sm text-warmgray-800 leading-relaxed"
                        >
                            Real-time project synchronization, shared Kanban
                            visibility, and activity tracking built for
                            multi-user teams with secure JWT authentication.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-14">
                <h2
                    class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-warmgray-800 mb-4"
                >
                    My contribution
                </h2>
                <p
                    class="font-sans text-base text-warmgray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4"
                >
                    I contributed across the full stack — from UX strategy and
                    interface design through to frontend implementation and team
                    coordination. With a four-person team and a tight academic
                    timeline, everyone wore multiple hats, and I took ownership
                    of the product experience end to end.
                </p>
                <p
                    class="font-sans text-base text-warmgray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4"
                >
                    On the UX side I defined the user flows, designed the
                    conversational AI interface, and shaped how the Kanban board
                    would present AI-generated output. On the engineering side I
                    built the React frontend, integrating the AI middleware
                    responses into the board UI in real time.
                </p>
                <p
                    class="font-sans text-base text-warmgray-600 leading-relaxed"
                >
                    The UX documentation is being recreated in Figma as a formal
                    case study — the product shipped, but the design artifacts
                    are ongoing work.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-14">
                <h2
                    class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-warmgray-800 mb-4"
                >
                    What I learned
                </h2>
                <p
                    class="font-sans text-base text-warmgray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4"
                >
                    Shipping a full product in an academic sprint taught me a
                    lot about prioritization under real constraints. Design
                    documentation got deprioritized in favor of shipping — a
                    tradeoff I understood at the time and am now correcting.
                </p>
                <p
                    class="font-sans text-base text-warmgray-600 leading-relaxed"
                >
                    More importantly, SmartBoardAI confirmed something I already
                    believed: the best product experiences come from people who
                    understand both sides of the stack. Designing the AI
                    interaction layer and then building it myself meant the
                    final product matched the intent in ways that are hard to
                    achieve across a handoff.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-16">
                <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-6">
                    <h2
                        class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-warmgray-800"
                    >
                        See it in action
                    </h2>
                    <a
                        href="https://github.com/Green-Depaul/SmartBoardAI"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener noreferrer"
                        class="font-mono text-sm text-rust-700 underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-rust-600 transition-colors"
                    >
                        View on GitHub →
                    </a>
                </div>
                <div
                    class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-warmgray-300"
                    style="height:480px"
                >
                    <iframe
                        src="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1tfgg1qeHmOAg4lOstlKkUsjcT85ITCST/preview"
                        width="100%"
                        height="100%"
                        allowfullscreen
                        loading="lazy"
                        title="SmartBoardAI demo video"
                        class="border-0"></iframe>
                </div>
            </section>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-16">
                <div class="bg-warmgray-200 rounded-lg p-6">
                    <p
                        class="font-mono text-xs text-rust-700 uppercase tracking-widest mb-3"
                    >
                        Frontend
                    </p>
                    <p class="font-sans text-sm text-warmgray-800">
                        React, TypeScript, Vite
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-warmgray-200 rounded-lg p-6">
                    <p
                        class="font-mono text-xs text-rust-700 uppercase tracking-widest mb-3"
                    >
                        Backend
                    </p>
                    <p class="font-sans text-sm text-warmgray-800">
                        Java Spring Boot, MySQL, JWT
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-warmgray-200 rounded-lg p-6">
                    <p
                        class="font-mono text-xs text-rust-700 uppercase tracking-widest mb-3"
                    >
                        AI Middleware
                    </p>
                    <p class="font-sans text-sm text-warmgray-800">
                        Python FastAPI, Together.AI SDK
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="pt-0">
                <a
                    href="/"
                    class="font-mono text-sm text-warmgray-500 hover:text-warmgray-800 transition-colors"
                    >← Back to home</a
                >
            </div>
        </article>
    </div>
</Layout>

<style>
    .page-reveal {
        animation: rise 0.6s ease-out both;
    }
    @keyframes rise {
        from {
            opacity: 0;
            transform: translateY(12px);
        }
        to {
            opacity: 1;
            transform: translateY(0);
        }
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .page-reveal {
            animation: none;
        }
    }
</style>
